  "worked_solution": "We start by sketching the solutions to the two inequalities separately:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191341/assets/7217f3db8adcbafdec9598e3c933fe1091e0abe9cabbdab57cca9cfb2d6cbb07.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191341/assets/690bb39741f157b12583ffffb75e47bcc171e04b7082f09005025f333807a234.png)\n\nThe common set of values consists of the values that are in both intervals. So, it can be graphed by finding where the two intervals overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191341/assets/d6ab3f0c43897adf0ae1b063d4d1d2437ce6d8f08355ff9f07a1e3e861e451b3.png)\n\nTherefore, the common set of values is\n$[-3,1).$",
